  "question": {
    "text": "The volume of hydrogen liberated at STP by treating&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi></math>&nbsp;of magnesium with excess of hydrochloric acid is ......<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">L</mi></math>. Given Molar volume of gas is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>22</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">L</mi></math>&nbsp;at STP. Molar mass of magnesium is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>24</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi>mol</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math><br />&nbsp;",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [],
  "correctValue": "224",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>The stoichiometric equation of the reaction between magnesium and hydrogen chloride can be written as follows,</p><p>One mole magnesium can liberate one mole of hydrogen gas according to the following equation.</p><p>&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><munder><mi>Mg</mi><munder><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>mole</mi></mrow></munder></munder><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>HCl</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo><msub><mi>MgCl</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><munder><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>mole</mi></mrow></munder></math><br />Volume of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn></math>&nbsp;mole&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math>&nbsp;at <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mn>22</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">L</mi></math>&nbsp;<br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8756;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>1</mn></math>&nbsp;mole&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math>&nbsp;at STP will occupy&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>24</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">L</mi></math></p>",
